  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Centripetal force will be provided by the spring force. Let the elongation in the spring be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, then we can&nbsp;write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, required tension will be<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
